From 0f2c79b767ae44eaff33285d7e288eccddc72ea0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeffrey Effendy <jeffreyeffendy@meta.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Feb 2026 07:43:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/63] [cvd-tool] Set device virtio-tablet-pci for mac host to
 enable using host cursor

Summary:
** Context **

This is part of resolving user request where user experience is degrading due to host mouse cursor is grabbed when interacting with QEMU UI window and needing to press `ctrl+opt+g` to escape.

Previously, the experience with Goldfish QEMU was that user can use host cursor without switching to guest cursor. So, the same experience should be expected with Cuttlefish QEMU.

See [user feedback doc](https://fburl.com/gdoc/3a669dh0)

** Diff Content **

- Set cocoa UI to always show cursor whenever interacting with QEMU UI.
- Set device to `virtio-tablet-pci` so that the interaction is using absolute mode, which is set by `INPUT_EVENT_MASK_ABS` in https://fburl.com/code/3rdqimrp. This would allow auto grab/ungrab and using absolute coordinate and not relative to the QEMU window.

Test Plan:
With device set, now we can use host mouse to interact with QEMU UI.

Build host tools on mac
```
mkdir -p ~/cvd-tools && cd ~/cvd-tools
repo init -u ssh://git-ro.vip.facebook.com/data/gitrepos/aosp/manifest.git \
  --repo-url=ssh://git.vip.facebook.com/data/gitrepos/osmeta/external/repo.git \
  --repo-branch=master \
  --current-branch --no-repo-verify --no-tags -b releases-nucleus-16.0-tiki-adhoc-cf-darwin-host-tools-system \
  --no-clone-bundle
repo sync -c -d --no-tags --force-sync -j12
. build/envsetup.sh
lunch aosp_cf_arm64_phone-userdebug
m out/host/darwin-x86/cvd-host_package.tar.gz
```

Make sure QEMU change is applied D93701930

Get emulator, modify the script to point to the local qemu, and start emulator
```
device device virtual -t device --cache-only
cd greatwhite_cf_emu_arm64-27580000003761-742834115373444
ln -s ~/cvd-tools/out/host/darwin-x86/cvd-host_package/* .
sed -i '' 's/{macos_qemu_path}/\/Users\/jeffreyeffendy\/qemu\/build/g' start_cuttlefish.py
./start_cuttlefish.py --enable_audio=false
```
https://pxl.cl/8VSzM

